Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 39 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  100    POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENSIVELY PRESENT AT THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Lymphatic and vascular invasion are not identified  Estrogen and progesterone receptors are ordered  Diagnosis by  Deborah S  Fleischhacker  MD ScD Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 52                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm oval portion of fibroadipose tissue  inked and sectioned to reval a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm area near one end which consists of dense fibrous tissue extending to the inked margin  Entirely submitted as follows  SECTION CODE  A B  Fibrous area  C F  Remainder  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT  BIOPSY  FOCALLY FIRM PARENCHYMA  BUT NO DISCRETE MASS IDENTIFIED  AWAIT PERMANENT SECTIONS  O R  Resident  Daniel D  Koelliker  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
