rminations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a modified radical mastectomy specimen  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm in greatest dimension  A skin ellipse with central nipple is attached with a long stitch at one end of the skin ellipse  and a short stitch ninety degrees away  The long stitch is parallel to an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm fibroadipose appendage to the bulk of the specimen  Two small fragments of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  6 0cm in greatest dimension are received  A central area of hard  irregularly outlined  white tan tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm in greatest dimension  0 9cm from the closest  deep  resection margin  The rest of the parenchyma is unremarkable  Representative sections of the hard mass are in A E  Representative sections of adjacent areas of breast parenchyma are in F J  Ten lymph nodes from the  appendage  of the specimen parallel to the long stitch range in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest dimensions  A section of each node is in K M  Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
