ola with a central unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan pink nipple  There is a2 7 x 0 1cm healed linear scar at the 6 o clock position that comes to 5 6cm of the nipple  Located 0 2cm inferior to the scar is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm tan brown papular skin lesion which comes to 2 0cm of the skin margin  Also noted are two additional tan brown crusted flap skin lesions measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm and REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  These lesions come to REMOVED_DATE and 0 6cm of the scar  respectively  These lesions are REMOVED_DATE and 1 8cm of the inferior skin margin  respectively  The anterior resection margin is inked blue  the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm cavity containing tan red serous sanguinous fluid  The cavity is located in the mid inferior breast tissue and comes to 3 0cm of the posterior margin  Surrounding the cavity is diffuse yellow orange discoloration consistent with fat necrosis and hemorrhage  Additional sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm indurated gray pink nodule at the 12 o clock position that is 0 2cm of the anterior margin  This nodule is located greater than 2 0cm superolateral to the cavity  The remaining cut surface shows diffusely dense  nodular gray white fibrous tissue with no other discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Sectioning of the upper outer quadrant reveals numerous tan pink lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Previous biopsy site  with closest posterior margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Indurated nodule at 12 o clock position  entirely submitted    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three lymph nodes bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lymph nodes  in toto   Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDE