Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 01 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  90   POSSIBLY INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  AND EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  10   CONFINED TO THE REGION SURROUNDING THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 55                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm fragment  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan pink  firm  stellate mass abutting the inked resection margin  No frozen done  The nodule is submitted entirely in A and B and the remainder of specimen in C through J  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS    RIGHT BREAST   LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA BUT TOO SMALL TO FROZEN     1CM   O R  Resident  FANG FANG  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST  BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
