yond the region of the invasive carcinoma  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  1 to 2  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Full panel requested on the 0 5cm nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    repeat Her 2 requested on the previously biopsied 1 0cm nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    See also  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  1  MULTIPLE SMALL FOCI OF INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  PRESENT AT THE INKED NEW MARGIN  2  FOCAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENDING TO THE INKED NEW MARGIN  3  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   NOTE  The foci of invasive carcinoma in this specimen resemble the larger tumor in the main excision  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left breast lumpectomy  short   superior  long   lateral   is an REMOVED_DATE  A P  x REMOVED_DATE  M L  x REMOVED_DATE  S I cm breast excision specimen oriented with a short stitch superior and a long stitch left lateral  2 needle localization wires are present in the specimen  both of which pass into the medial aspect  one anteriorly and one posteriorly  The wires are removed and the specimen is inked per protocol as follows  Superior   blue  inferior   black  medial   green  lateral   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the anterior posterior axis into 11 slices numbered from posterior to anterior  An ill defined tan pink area of fibrosis  cystic change  and nodularity is present in slice  6  which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm and approaches to 0 7cm from the inferior margin  1 5cm from the superior margin  0 5cm from the lateral margin  2 0cm from the medial margin  3 5cm from the posterior margin  and 3 4cm from the anterior margin  A biopsy tract is passing through this area and a clip is identified in slice  5 adjacent to the mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  1  representa