tive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a breast lumpectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm containing two sutures  A short suture designates the superior margin and a long suture designates the lateral  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 3cm hemorrhagic biopsy site with an adjacent 1 4cm firm  tan white area grossly abutting the inked margins anteriorly  The biopsy site comes within 1 5cm of the deep margin which is overinked blue  The parenchyma surrounding the biopsy cavity is composed predominantly of dense  white  fibrous tissue with no additional anomalies  SECTION CODE A  FX  1  residue  B C  Biopsy cavity in relation to closest anterior margin  D  Biopsy cavity in relation to deep margin  inked blue   E  Remainder of biopsy cavity with adjacent firm nodule abutting anterior margin  F  Representative section of fibrous tissue from medial aspect  G  Representative section of fibrous tissue from lateral aspect  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are 3 additional specimens  Labeled  additional shaved margins  are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in aggregate  The specimens are sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes H through M  Labeled  additional axillary tissue  is a segment of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMO