Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Resident  Devon Gimbel  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 33 year old woman with a new cluster of calcifications seen on a recent mammogram  The patient s mother had breast cancer at age 36  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPE WITH COMEDO NECROSIS  SEE TABLE  1 AND NOTE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU TUMOR SIZE  Microscopic foci involving 1 of 6 blocks spanning at least 0 6cm  GRADE  2  CALCIFICATIONS  Limited to the carcinoma in situ  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Positive at the anterior margin of the specimen along a broad front  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  A panel of immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  p63  myosin and calponin were performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The immunostaining pattern highlights the myoepithelial layer in areas of ductal carcinoma in situ and supports the diagnosis  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression will be reported in an addendum  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast excision   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm excision specimen with one needle localization wire in place and accompanied b