Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Michael W Lawlor  M D   Ph D  Reports To  CHARLES MASON FERGUSON  M D  CLINICAL DATA  History of invasive carcinoma and DCIS in right breast  DCIS was close to surgical margin  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm portion of breast tissue with a single stitch designating medial  two stitches designating inferior  and an attached skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The skin ellipse contains a REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm well healed scar which is located 0 8cm from the medial margin of the skin ellipse  0 6cm from the lateral margin of the skin ellipse  0 7cm from the superior margin of the skin ellipse  and 0 7cm from the inferior margin of the skin ellipse  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior  black  superior green  inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm biopsy cavity  which is partially filled with clotted blood  The cavity is located 0 4cm from the medial margin  1 3cm from the lateral margin  0 8cm from the superior margin  1 0cm from the inferior margin  and 0 8cm from the posterior margin  and 0 7cm from the anterior margin  No masses and other cysts are noted within the specimen  Representative section from the biopsy cavity and the posterior margin are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Other representative sections including the other margins are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Michael W Lawlor M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Michael W Lawlor M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 19 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN ONE OF EIGHT LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The metastasis is confined to the lymph node  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   HIGHEST    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 41                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 23     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR C ERB  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  PROTEIN AS REPORTED BY IMPATH BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 MAY 97 at 09 00     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Staining for hormone receptor proteins was repeated at the patient s request  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 MAY 97 at 09 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right modified mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm unoriented right breast  with a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable nipple with no incisions  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm hemorrhagic area approximately 2 0cm from the skin ellipse  grossly abutting the closest inked surface  Approximately 8 0cm away from the hemorrhagic area is a firm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm nodule sectioned to reveal an ill defined  stellate hard white mass surrounded by hemorrhage focally extending to within 0 1cm of a deep margin  The remaining parenchyma consists of fibrofatty tissue  with focal areas of hemorrhage  Section Code  A G  representative sections of ill defined hemorrhagic area  H K  representative sections of firm stellate white nodule  L  representative section of firm white areas surrounding biopsy cavity  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right axillary nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of adipose tissue  dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 2cm  Representative sections of lymph nodes submitted in M through P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Highest axillary nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of adipose tissue  dissected to reveal a tan brown lymph node  which is bisected and submitted entirely in cassette Q  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  Alisa B  Goldberg M D  PART A  RIGHT MASTECTOMY PART B  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES PART C  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE   HIGHEST    report_end  , Unchecked.
