eep superior  double stitch at deep inferior   consists of a 3 x 0 5cm skin ellipse with a corrugated surface and an area that looks like it could be a surgical scar attached to a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm fibrofatty lumpectomy specimen  There are two sutures at one pole of the lumpectomy specimen and there is one suture at the opposite pole with a skin ellipse located approximately halfway between them  The specimen is inked as follows  the deep portion is inked black  the superficial surface is inked blue  the lateral surface is inked yellow  the medial surface is inked green  The specimen is sectioned in the superior to inferior direction  Sectioning revealed a gray tan area of dense fibrosis extending to the margin  There is also a central cavity  filled with hemorrhage  0 5cm across  and 0 6cm from the nearest margin  The cassettes are as follows  A  Entire submitted epidermis  B J  Entire lumpectomy specimen from superior to inferior tip  Resident  MINDY J  HULL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  RE EXCISION , Unchecked.
