Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 06 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  SINGLE FOCUS SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM FOCALLY PRESENT AT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM OF A RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CONFINED TO THE MASS  NOTE  Invasion of lymphatic vessels or blood vessels is not seen  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 14 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 AUG 98 at 15 56 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm unoriented yellow fibroadipose tissue with a localization wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 7cm white stellate firm mass abutting the inked margin  The mass is submitted entirely in A C  Representative sections of unremarkable breast tissue are submitted in D E  Resident  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA CLOSE TO A SURGICAL MARGIN  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
