Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 04 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  1   MASS   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of invasive carcinoma  BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  2   CALCIFICATIONS   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM IN TISSUE SECTION AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of the stroma  blood vessels  and lymphatic vessels is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 20                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   MASS    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 58    REVISED REMOVED_DATE        RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast lesion  are two fragments of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The larger specimen  with two wires  is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 6cm well circumscribed tan mass  0 2cm from the margin and the second mass 0 5cm at the margin  The second  smaller  specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast tissue  Section code  A B  first mass C  second mass D F  additional sections from first fragment G J  second fragment  entirely submitted Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST   MASS   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LEFT BREAST   CALCIFICATIONS   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
