ratin 7  and pankeratin on three tissue levels support the diagnosis  Sections of the main breast excision  part B  reveal diffuse invasive lobular carcinoma arising in a background of extensive lobular carcinoma in situ  Both the invasive and in situ lobular carcinoma are present at the posterior margin of the specimen  There is extensive artifact with stromal retraction present which limits assessment for the presence of lymphatic vessel invasion  however  a few foci with definitive lymphatic vessel invasion as well as peri neural invasion are identified  Immunohistochemical stains for e cadherin were performed on  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The e cadherin stain is negative in areas of invasive and in situ lobular carcinoma and supports the diagnosis  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left axilla sentinel node count    REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm lymph node which is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1 and now entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   is a 13 x 13 x 2cm left simple mastectomy specimen oriented with a stitch designating 12 o clock  The specimen was weighed at the surgeon s request in the Frozen Section Lab and the total was 163 g  The overlying is a 3 x 2cm skin ellipse with a REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm nipple which is grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  Upon sectioning there is an ill defined cavity surrounded by fibrosis and measuring 1 x 1 x 0 5cm in the left upper outer quadrant which is grossly 0 1cm from the posterior resection margin and 0 3cm from the anterior resection margin  Adjacent to the biopsy cavity  there is a 3 x 3 x 2cm ill defined fibrotic mass with numerous firmer nodules which abut posterior resection margin and are 0 5cm from the anterior resection margin  The rest of br