oses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast cancer   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm yellow white irregular fibrofatty tissue  with a short stitch designating anterior  a long stitch designating lateral  and a bowtie designating cephalad  There is a localization wire in place  which enters in through the anterior aspect  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  inferior yellow  superior green  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm tan white firm mass  which is focally hemorrhagic and is surrounded by both white fibrous tissue and yellow chalky adipose tissue  This mass comes to within 0 8cm of the anterior margin  1 4cm of the posterior margin  1 5cm from the inferior margin  2 0cm from the superior margin and greater than 2 5cm from the remaining margins  The remainder of the cut surface consists of yellow adipose tissue with minimal white fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of mass to inferior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Radial sections to lateral margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Radial sections to medial margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative uninvolved section  medial to tumor  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node conglomerate 220   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm yellow irregular fatty tissue  within which 4 lymph nodes are identified  The lymph nodes are submitted in entirety as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes  Gross Dictation by Michael R Tan  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Christine Garcia M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Review by Christine Garcia M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Christine Garcia