Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 09 25 CLINICAL DATA  Patient presents with infiltrating ductal carcinoma in the tail of the breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT     INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED   GRADE 2 3   PRESENT AT SEVERAL DEEP  POSTERIOR  RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE     BIOPSY SITE WITH FIBROSIS  GRANULATION TISSUE  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  NOTE  Lymphatic invasion is present  No in situ carcinoma is identified in this specimen  AXILLARY CONTENTS  RIGHT   METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA IS PRESENT IN 4 OF 21 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 09                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed 