 of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 AUG 94 at 15 07     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 8 5cm tan skin ellipse with a 3 0cm in diameter inverted tan nipple as well as attached 8 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm tan yellow axillary fatty tail  There is a long stitch at what appears to be the lateral aspect and a short stitch that appears to be at the superior aspect  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm tan  firm  irregular  ill defined mass present  1 8cm from the closest deep margin and 8 0cm from the medial margin  The rest of the breast parenchyma is tan yellow and fatty with irregular  ill defined  fibrotic areas present throughout the specimen  Multiple tan  semifirm  unremarkable lymph nodes  measuring in greatest diameter from 0 2cm to 1 1cm are present in the axillary tail  Representative sections of the mass is frozen as FX 1  SECTION CODE  A  FX 1  representative mass   B  closest soft tissue margin  deep  C F  representative sections of tumor  