Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 49 CLINICAL DATA  The patient presents with a right breast mass  History of small cell carcinoma in the left breast diagnosed in  REMOVED_CASE_ID                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 1 3   100   EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The focus of infiltrating carcinoma measures approximately 0 5cm in greatest dimension  No blood vessel or lymphatic vessel invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 16                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assa