r  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm previous biopsy site which is centrally cystic and filled with clotted blood  Surrounding the cyst is white fibrous tissue and fat necrosis  The fibrous tissue extends from the biopsy cavity to the surrounding margins in a stellate fashion  0 6cm from the biopsy cavity is a 0 8cm tan cystic mass which is located 0 3cm from the nearest margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is approximately 85  fatty and 15  fibrous  The fibrous areas are dense  and cystic  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A D  Biopsy cavity E  Adjacent mass F L  Fibrous areas  Gross Description by  SHANNON SCHUTZ Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
